{"kind":"request","text":"Choose and specify attention delivery while the person is absent\n\nBuilder/design: deliver notes/2026-10-03-absent-attention.md. C3 already owes durable agent attention and C5 its browser inbox; choose the missing beyond-closed-browser delivery path through independent product/authority review. Compare opt-in Web Push or another explicitly authorized channel with inbox-only return. Specify consent, device/channel owner, current access/revocation, private payload minimization, provider/operator cost, exact Room/task/attention decision anchors, duplicate suppression, reconnect/catch-up, expiry, pause/budget and failure. Notifications are advisory and carry no control/review authority; opening authenticates to current exact attention. Distinguish this from agent trigger/wake design 24711ceb. Explicitly decide disclosure of queued alerts after device/channel revocation; a delivery already accepted by an external provider cannot be assumed recalled.\n\nCommissioned under independently approved experience map a259c26d and adopted scope cf116410, planned at main e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967. This request delivers the design/specification and implementing-lane handoff. Planner will commission its implementation separately after exact design review and adoption; no new protocol/runtime decision is adopted here.\n\nC1 private/resource authority, C3/C5 durable attention and C4 device lifecycle. Channel decision remains proposed until review/adoption; no first-Jam gate.","body":{"conditions":"Design a bounded absent-A/authorized-B case: opted-in authorized destination alerted, B opens specific attention, authenticates/responds normally, delivery failure leaves durable inbox attention, revoked device/channel loses the chosen access/payload. Inbox-only is explicitly reduced experience until chosen delivery implemented. Independent design review/adoption first, then separately commissioned C3/C5 implementation integration; no new social/chat 